warning[self_assignment]: `width` is assigned to itself
  --> tests/lint/self_assignment/bad.jai:11:5
   |
11 |     width = width;
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: this does nothing; was another value or target meant? (after `using`, both sides name the same field)
   |
10       width := 4;
11 -     width = width;
12       s.height = s.height;
   |
   = note: `self_assignment` is `warn` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/self_assignment

warning[self_assignment]: `s.height` is assigned to itself
  --> tests/lint/self_assignment/bad.jai:12:5
   |
12 |     s.height = s.height;
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: this does nothing; was another value or target meant? (after `using`, both sides name the same field)
   |
11       width = width;
12 -     s.height = s.height;
13       print("% %\n", s, width);
   |
   = note: `self_assignment` is `warn` by default
